course: dictionary
lesson: 10177
title: One word, two meanings: tiger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word tiger can mean two different things. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use. «The thylacine, or Tasmanian tiger, was a striped meat-eating marsupial that looked like a dog.» Here tiger is part of a name, and the clues marsupial and looked like a dog show it is not a cat at all.
explain: «The tiger is not on fire: its orange stripes seem to glow like flames in the dark forest.» This tiger is the big wild cat. The clues are orange stripes and a dark forest. The sentence even says it is not on fire, so the writer wants you to picture the animal, not a burning thing.
explain: Always check your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If you say «A tiger is a fierce, brave person» in place of tiger in the stripes sentence, it does not fit. So the animal meaning is the right one.
fact: A tiger is a very large wild cat with orange fur and black stripes, which lives in Asia.
fact: A tiger can also mean a fierce, brave or energetic person.
fact: A female tiger is called a tigress.
fact: «The Tasmanian tiger» was a striped meat-eating marsupial, not a cat, and the last known one died in a zoo in 1936.
fact: «No two tigers have the same stripes», so scientists can tell them apart from camera photos.
exercise: «A tiger's skin is striped under the fur, and no two tigers have the same stripes.» What is a tiger in this sentence? | *A large wild cat | A kind of shark | A striped marsupial that looked like a dog | A fierce, brave person
exercise: «The thylacine, or Tasmanian tiger, was a striped meat-eating marsupial that looked like a dog.» What kind of animal was the Tasmanian tiger? | A bird that could fly | *A striped meat-eating marsupial | A cat like the one in the forest | A tiger shark
exercise: Coach says, «Ana is a tiger in the race today.» What does tiger mean here? | A striped animal from Tasmania | A large wild cat with orange fur | *A fierce, brave or energetic person | A type of shark
test: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother.» What may the white spots help cubs do? | Hide from the camera | *Follow their mother | Swim faster than their mother | Fly through the trees
test: «The tiger is not on fire: its orange stripes seem to glow like flames in the dark forest.» Why does the writer say it is not on fire? | *To help you picture the animal and its glowing stripes | Because tigers never go near fire | To say the tiger is a fierce person | Because the forest is wet
exam: Which sentence uses tiger to mean a fierce, brave or energetic person? | *Our goalkeeper is a real tiger when the ball comes near | The thylacine was a marsupial that looked like a dog | The tiger ran through the grass at dawn | Tigers live in Asia and swim well
